{
	title: 'Block ids in model text are links',
	spec: 'A block id in model text (answers and thinking, outside code), such as #t125 or #u12, is a link to that block\'s card: on the web, the task 0z address /<session id>#<id> in the same tab; in the terminal, an OSC 8 hyperlink to <webUrl>/<session id>#<id> when webUrl is known, else plain text. "<session id>#<id>" links to a block in another session. Only a kind letter (task 9p) followed by a number counts, so "#1" or "#fff" stays text. Only ids that name an existing block in the target session become links; invented ids stay plain text. Trailing punctuation follows task hb\'s rule. The rule lives in src/common, as an autolink step beside hb\'s, and both clients use it. Tests: an id inside code stays text; an id beyond the session\'s last block stays text; "#t5." links #t5 without the period.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		"markdown.parse(text, streaming, links): scan() links #<kind><n>[.i] or <session>#<id> (not after a word character, not followed by one) when links returns an href. markdown.blockLinks(session, key, known): an own-session id links only when older than the item showing it (a writer can cite only blocks it saw), so no client state is needed; another session's id links when known(session), which the clients don't pass yet, so those stay text. Web in-app hrefs (starting /) open in the same tab."
	],
	needs: ['9p', '0z', 'hb', 'fn', 'c2t'],
